# Horde AMI Build Guide

Generated by `fabrica horde ami build` for Horde **{{ .Version }}** ({{ .Install }} install) in `{{ .Region }}`.

## Overview

`fabrica horde create` requires a pre-baked AMI. A successful **docker install**
bake produces an AMI that contains:

| Component       | Detail                                                        | systemd unit   |
|-----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|
| Ubuntu          | 22.04 LTS (jammy)                                              | —              |
| AWS CLI v2      | `/usr/local/bin/aws` (installed by the bake; see SSM notes)    | —              |
| Docker CE       | installed, enabled, with the Compose v2 plugin                 | `docker`       |
| Compose stack   | `/etc/horde/docker-compose.yml` (mongodb + redis + horde)      | —              |
| Horde config    | `/etc/horde/globals.json` (Build plugin enabled) + `/etc/horde/server.json` | — |
| Horde server    | `fabrica-horde-server:{{ .Version }}` baked from the account ECR mirror of `ghcr.io/epicgames/horde-server:{{ .Version }}`, plus `mongo:7.0` / `redis:7.2` | `horde` |

The `horde` unit starts the stack with `docker compose up -d` from `/etc/horde`,
and Fabrica's cloud-init does the same — the generated component and Packer
template write the compose file, configs, and the systemd unit to exactly those
paths and bake the images, so the generated AMI serves the jobs API
(`GET /api/v1/jobs`) out of the box.

A **native install** bake instead installs .NET 8, MongoDB 7.0, and Redis and
syncs the Horde binary from S3 (unit working directory `/opt/horde`).

Fabrica's cloud-init only configures and starts services — it does not install
software.

Amazon SSM Agent is required. The generated component and Packer template enable
the deb or snap unit (installing the snap if neither is present) and fail closed
if the agent cannot be enabled. Verify SSM registration on a private subnet
before recording a known-good AMI.

## Generated Files

- `image-builder-recipe.json` — AWS EC2 Image Builder recipe (input to `aws imagebuilder create-image-recipe`)
- `component.yaml` — Image Builder Component document (input to `aws imagebuilder create-component`)
{{- if .IncludePacker }}
- `packer.pkr.hcl` — Packer HCL template (use with `packer init` + `packer build`)
{{- end }}
- `build-guide.md` — this file

