## Verifying the AMI

After launching a test instance from your new AMI, verify the services are
running and the jobs API is accessible. **A health-only Horde (responds on
`:5000` but no jobs API) will cause `fabrica horde submit` and `fabrica ci
trigger` to fail with 404 errors.**

{{ if eq .Install "docker" -}}
### Docker compose stack

```bash
# Start the stack
cd /etc/horde && docker compose up -d
docker compose ps

# Health check — must return 200
curl -sf http://localhost:5000/ && echo "Health: OK"

# Jobs API — must NOT return 404
# Acceptable: 200 (empty list), 401 (auth challenge)
# FAIL: 404 with empty body or "route missing"
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "Jobs API: HTTP %{http_code}\n" \
  http://localhost:5000/api/v1/jobs

# Container health — all three should show "healthy"
docker ps --filter "name=horde"
```
{{ else -}}
### Native install

```bash
# Service status
systemctl is-enabled mongod redis-server horde

# Health check — must return 200
curl -sf http://localhost:5000/ && echo "Health: OK"

# Jobs API — must NOT return 404
# Acceptable: 200 (empty list), 401 (auth challenge)
# FAIL: 404 with empty body or "route missing" — do not bake this AMI
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "Jobs API: HTTP %{http_code}\n" \
  http://localhost:5000/api/v1/jobs

# Database check
mongosh --eval "db.adminCommand('ping')"
ls -la /etc/horde/
```
{{ end -}}

Then verify Fabrica can build the provisioning plan:

```bash
fabrica horde create --dry-run
```

## Verifying over SSM (dash and PATH gotchas)

SSM `AWS-RunShellScript` runs your payload under **dash**, not bash. A bare
`set -o pipefail` dies at line 1 (`Illegal option -o pipefail`), and the stock
jammy PATH for SSM sessions does **not** include `/usr/local/bin`, so the baked
`/usr/local/bin/aws` is invisible to bare `aws`. Run SSM commands explicitly
under bash and use the full CLI path:

```bash
aws ssm send-command --document-name AWS-RunShellScript \
  --targets "Keys=instanceIds,Values=<instance-id>" \
  --parameters 'commands=[#!/bin/bash
set -eu
export PATH="/usr/local/bin:$PATH"
systemctl is-enabled horde docker
/usr/local/bin/aws sts get-caller-identity >/dev/null && echo "aws CLI v2 OK"
cd /etc/horde && docker compose ps]'
```

Notes:

- Use `#!/bin/bash` + `set -eu` (never bare `set -o pipefail` under dash).
- Call the AWS CLI as `/usr/local/bin/aws` (or export `PATH` first) — it is
  installed by the bake but not on the SSM session PATH.
- A healthy `GET /api/v1/jobs` over SSM must be `200` or `401`, **not** `404` —
  a 404 means the AMI was baked without the job controllers.

## Common Pitfalls

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `mongod` not healthy at cloud-init time | Add startup readiness checks to the AMI |
| `horde` unit not found | Unit must be named exactly `horde` |
| `/etc/horde/Server.json` not read | Set `Horde__DataDir=/etc/horde` in the service env |
| `redis` unit not found | Fabrica tries `redis-server` then `redis`; ensure one exists |
| AMI in wrong region | Re-copy the AMI to each deployment region |
| Architecture mismatch | Build the AMI on the same instance family (x86_64 for m7i) |
| Image Builder rejects the recipe | The placeholder `REPLACE_WITH_CUSTOM_COMPONENT_ARN` was not substituted |
| Bake fails at the ECR pull with `no basic auth credentials` | `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken` needs `Resource: "*"`; repo-scoped it returns AccessDenied |
| `docker pull ghcr.io/...` fails with 401 | GHCR image is private — mirror it to ECR (docker prerequisites) and bake from ECR with the instance role |
| SSM command dies at line 1 (`Illegal option -o pipefail`) | Run under `#!/bin/bash`; dash does not support `pipefail` |
| `aws: command not found` inside an SSM session | Use `/usr/local/bin/aws` or `export PATH="/usr/local/bin:$PATH"` |
| Stock jammy has no `unzip` / `aws` CLI | The generated component installs both (AWS CLI v2 via zip + `unzip`); if baking manually, install them first |
